        "original_id": "c631aa4a-b723-5df2-a41f-33e24278316f",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Juan Pablo Montoya, Rubens Barrichello, Marc Gené, Ralf Schumacher\n- Products: Williams FW25, Williams car, Ferrari car\n- Events: 2003 Italian Grand Prix, 2003 Formula One season\n- Places: Monza, Lesmo 1 corner\n\nFacts:\n- In the 2003 Formula One season, three drivers drove the Williams FW25.\n- Before the 2003 Italian Grand Prix, Ralf Schumacher suffered a major testing accident at Monza's Lesmo 1 corner.\n- At the 2003 Italian Grand Prix, Marc Gené replaced Ralf Schumacher in the Williams FW25.\n- At the 2003 Italian Grand Prix, Juan Pablo Montoya finished second in a Williams car.\n- At the 2003 Italian Grand Prix, Rubens Barrichello finished third in the other Ferrari.\n- Rubens Barrichello, born on 23 May 1972, is a Brazilian racing driver.\n- Rubens Barrichello competed in Formula One between 1993 and 2011.\n- Rubens Barrichello scored 11 Grands Prix wins and 68 podiums in Formula One.",
